Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Mon Nov 23 13:57:25 2026 -0500

    fix(install): stamp the chosen release version into the release-mode wrapper. Addresses TJ-DF-076.
    
    Release mode downloaded terminal_jail-<version>-py3-none-any.whl, verified its
    SHA256SUMS entry, and installed the wheel's bundled wrapper verbatim — but
    that bundled copy ships VERSION_DEFAULT="" and the installed layout has no
    pyproject.toml next to the script to fall back on, so the installed CLI
    reported an empty --version forever ("terminal-jail "), while every checkout
    install stamped the pyproject version.
    
    - install.sh: after the shared shebang/shape checks (so a bad shebang keeps
      its own message and the payload is already validated), release mode now
      stamps VERSION_DEFAULT="<chosen>" into the verified payload via awk (already
      a hard release-mode dependency through the SHA256SUMS parse; the version
      rides in as an awk -v variable, never interpolated program text). A wheel
      whose bundled wrapper lost the stampable line is refused loudly (format
      drift fails closed) and the stamp temp writes through .terminal-jail.$$.stamped
      with a rename, covered by the existing cleanup trap.
    - install.sh: TERMINAL_JAIL_VERSION is shape-checked at parse time (PEP 440-ish
      charset [0-9A-Za-z._+-], leading 'v' accepted/stripped as before); every
      quote, sed metacharacter, and newline lies outside the charset, so no splice
      surface can be turned into code or a broken wrapper. Mirrors the
      TERMINAL_JAIL_REQUIRE_TIER refusal (exit 1, nothing written).
    - plugin/test_install.py: FAKE_BINARY now mirrors the real bundled wrapper's
      version path (VERSION_DEFAULT="" + VERSION resolution + --version dispatch),
      and four regression tests cover: chosen-version stamp end to end via the
      installed binary's --version with a scratch HOME and controlled wheel
      fixture (checksum-OK ordering asserted), 'v'-prefixed selection stamping the
      stripped version, parse-time refusal of a metacharacter-carrying version
      with nothing written, and the no-stampable-line fail-closed gate. All four
      demonstrated RED against the pre-fix installer and GREEN after.
    
    Local-mode behavior and the TJ-GAP-087 absolute-path release contract are
    unchanged: checkout installs still stamp from pyproject.toml, absolute-path
    invocations with TERMINAL_JAIL_USE_RELEASE=1 still see release assets only,
    and the default-path installer behavior is identical for every valid version.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
